From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 23:15:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] libressl: define htobe32/htobe64 on Windows when endian.h exists

The Windows build (MSYS2 clang64, newest packages) stopped in libressl:
"call to undeclared function 'htobe32'" (and htobe64) in
crypto/crypto_internal.h. Newer MinGW-w64 headers ship an <endian.h>, so
libressl's CMake sets HAVE_ENDIAN_H. Its compat endian.h never includes the
system header on Windows, and its own Windows definitions were only used
without HAVE_ENDIAN_H, so nothing defined them. They are now defined on
Windows whenever htobe32 isn't defined yet.

libressl is a submodule, so this patch changes a file inside it (git apply
only, like 0074).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FYz3krf43qKGY6aS2Z5snz
---
 externals/libressl/include/compat/endian.h | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/externals/libressl/include/compat/endian.h b/externals/libressl/include/compat/endian.h
index d9f7eb2..e4c6393 100644
--- a/externals/libressl/include/compat/endian.h
+++ b/externals/libressl/include/compat/endian.h
@@ -60,7 +60,11 @@
 #define be64toh(x) OSSwapBigToHostInt64(x)
 #endif /* __APPLE__ && !HAVE_ENDIAN_H */
 
-#if defined(_WIN32) && !defined(HAVE_ENDIAN_H)
+/*
+ * On Windows the system <endian.h> is never included above, so these are needed even when
+ * one exists (newer MinGW-w64 headers have it, which sets HAVE_ENDIAN_H).
+ */
+#if defined(_WIN32) && !defined(htobe32)
 #include <winsock2.h>
 
 #define be16toh(x) ntohs((x))
@@ -77,7 +81,7 @@
 #endif
 
 #define htobe64(x) ntohll((x))
-#endif /* _WIN32 && !HAVE_ENDIAN_H */
+#endif /* _WIN32 && !htobe32 */
 
 #ifdef __linux__
 #if !defined(betoh16)
-- 
2.43.0

